    "author": "Guillon",
    "body_normalized": "**System Information**\nOperating system: Windows-10-10.0.19045-SP0 64 Bits\nGraphics card: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 NVIDIA Corporation NVIDIA 595.79 Vulkan Backend\n\n**Blender Version**\nBroken: version: 5.1.0, branch: blender-v5.1-release, commit date: 2026-03-16 18:50, hash: `adfe2921d5f3`\nBroken: version: 5.0.0\nWorked: 4.5.8\n\n**Short description of error**\nWhen loading an image strip into the VSE, if the image file name contains eleven consecutive numbers, the image is not loaded and the strip is displayed with the error icon.\n\n**Exact steps for others to reproduce the error**\n1.- Open Blender.\n2.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n3.- Load an image file with the name \"1234567890\".\n4.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n5.- Load an image file with the name \"12345678901\".\n6.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n7.- Load an image file with the name \"12345a67890\".\n8.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n9.- Load an image file with the name \"12345a678901\".",
    "body_raw": "**System Information**\nOperating system: Windows-10-10.0.19045-SP0 64 Bits\nGraphics card: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 NVIDIA Corporation NVIDIA 595.79 Vulkan Backend\n\n**Blender Version**\nBroken: version: 5.1.0, branch: blender-v5.1-release, commit date: 2026-03-16 18:50, hash: `adfe2921d5f3`\nBroken: version: 5.0.0\nWorked: 4.5.8\n\n**Short description of error**\nWhen loading an image strip into the VSE, if the image file name contains eleven consecutive numbers, the image is not loaded and the strip is displayed with the error icon.\n\n**Exact steps for others to reproduce the error**\n1.- Open Blender.\n2.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n3.- Load an image file with the name \"1234567890\".\n4.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n5.- Load an image file with the name \"12345678901\".\n6.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n7.- Load an image file with the name \"12345a67890\".\n8.- In the VSE add an Image Strip.\n9.- Load an image file with the name \"12345a678901\".\n\n\n",
